# Environment Setup and Verification
# PicoRV32 Benchmarking: Environment Setup

## 1. Project Overview

This project aims to benchmark the PicoRV32 RISC-V processor core
and study its performance using software benchmarks and simulation.

This document records the initial environment checks and RISC-V
compiler verification performed on Ubuntu.

## 2. Development Environment

| Component | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| Operating System | Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS |
| Build System | GNU Make |
| Version Control | Git |
| Native Compiler | GCC |
| HDL Simulator | Icarus Verilog |
| Simulation Runtime | VVP |
| RISC-V Compiler | riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc |
| RISC-V Compiler Version | GCC 14.2.0 |

## 3. Project Directories

PicoRV32 source repository:

`~/picorv32`

Benchmarking repository:

`~/picorv32-benchmarking`

The PicoRV32 source and benchmarking documentation are maintained
in separate directories.

## 4. Environment Verification

The following development tools were found in the environment:

- Git
- GNU Make
- GCC
- Icarus Verilog (`iverilog`)
